  "conclusions": [
    "Load includes file verification, CPU parsing and allocations, yielded Editor waits, and GPU buffer allocations/uploads. It is not a CPU-only model inference path.",
    "Large constants use bounded GPU SetData before scheduling; smaller constants may be uploaded lazily. Load CPU/wall must not be described as all-weight GPU readiness.",
    "CloseAsync may await a pending canceled call; these receipts close after four completed calls. Their short release times do not qualify busy-session cancellation latency.",
    "Resource disposal has been asserted by the original tests, but return from CloseAsync does not measure when the graphics driver returns memory or finishes all GPU queues.",
    "Existing load/release GPU timings were not captured. Null is missing evidence, not zero GPU work, and cannot be reconstructed from CPU/wall or GPU-memory samples.",
    "A future load/release GPU probe must capture and calibrate the actual upload/resource-retirement scope without enclosing Task.Yield across frames in one synchronous marker or changing SDK scheduling."
  ],
